Subject: [PATCH 07/38] Interactive --watch view with table of contents

On a terminal, --watch now opens a full-screen view on the alternate screen
instead of printing the whole document (which left only its tail visible):

- scroll with j/k, arrows, PgUp/PgDn, space/b, g/G, Home/End
- t opens the table of contents in leaf's style (sections numbered 01..,
  subsections with a bullet, a single top heading treated as the title);
  Up/Down + Enter jumps to a section, t/Esc goes back
- 1-9 jumps straight to a section
- q/Esc quits; Ctrl+C restores the terminal
- re-renders on file change and terminal resize

Without a terminal (pipes) --watch behaves as before.
