From 50aa77320cf69c18888715f51fa17e2f431330cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sfslinux <sfslinux@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:13:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/38] Parse and lay out Markdown text like leaf
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Block level:
- lines of one paragraph stay together (source line breaks are kept,
  as in leaf) instead of becoming separate paragraphs
- paragraphs, list items and quotes are word-wrapped to the terminal
- indented lines continue the list item above
- consecutive "> " lines form one quote, drawn with a "▏" bar
- nested lists (•, ◦, ▪), ordered lists keep their start number,
  task items [ ] / [x] shown as ☐ / ☑
- setext headings (=== / ---), thematic breaks *** and * * *
- footnotes: [^x] becomes a superscript, notes listed at the end
- an unclosed ``` fence keeps its content; CRLF line endings

Inline:
- nested emphasis (**bold *italic* bold**) and ~~strikethrough~~,
  flattened into style bits on plain tokens
- no emphasis for "2 * 3" or snake_case_names; backslash escapes
- code spans with backticks inside (`` a ` b ``)
- images ![alt](src) and autolinks <https://...> as links
- table cells: "\|" and pipes inside `code` do not split

Headings are underlined like leaf: ═ for level 1, ─ below.

tests/parser_test.cpp covers the parser; run with ctest.
