--- /dev/null
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,95 @@
+# AGENTS.md
+
+TermMark: terminal Markdown viewer in C++17. No dependencies beyond the C++ standard library and
+POSIX (`ioctl`, `termios`, `poll`, `wcwidth`). The rendering target is [leaf](https://github.com/RivoLink/leaf):
+when in doubt about how something should look, do what `leaf --inline` does.
+
+## Layout
+
+| Path | What |
+|---|---|
+| `main.cpp` | CLI: `file.md`, `--watch`, `--guide`, `--help`, `--version` |
+| `include/parser/MarkdownParser.h`, `src/parser/MarkdownParser.cpp` | Markdown -> `Token` list (blocks) with `InlineToken` content |
+| `src/renderer/Renderer.cpp` | Tokens -> ANSI text on `std::cout`; table layout, code frames, word wrap, TOC, pager helpers |
+| `src/watch/watch.cpp` | `--watch`: full-screen pager on a terminal (scroll, `t` contents, `1-9`, `/` search), plain re-render loop otherwise |
+| `src/utils/` | file reading, hyperlink support detection, `--help` text (`cli_info.cpp`), `--guide` demo document |
+| `include/utils/TermStyle.h` | ANSI color/style constants; use these, not raw escapes |
+| `tests/parser_test.cpp` | parser checks (`CHECK` macro, works with `NDEBUG`) |
+
+## Build and test
+
+```sh
+cmake -S . -B build && cmake --build build && ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
+```
+
+Without cmake, the same with g++:
+
+```sh
+mkdir -p tmp
+g++ -std=c++17 -O1 -Wall -Iinclude main.cpp $(find src -name '*.cpp') -o tmp/termmark
+g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Iinclude tests/parser_test.cpp src/parser/MarkdownParser.cpp -o tmp/parser_test && tmp/parser_test
+```
+
+Put scratch files and binaries in `tmp/` (not committed) and delete them when done.
+
+## Checking output
+
+Layout depends on the terminal width, so check it in a pseudo-terminal of a known width and
+compare with leaf:
+
+```sh
+script -qec "stty cols 60; tmp/termmark file.md" /dev/null </dev/null | sed 's/\x1b\[[0-9;]*m//g'
+leaf --inline plain:60 file.md
+```
+
+Piped output (no terminal) is laid out for 80 columns, like leaf.
+
+For `--watch`, drive it in tmux and read the screen:
+
+```sh
+tmux -L t new-session -d -s t -x 90 -y 20 "tmp/termmark --watch file.md"
+tmux -L t send-keys -t t t Down Enter; tmux -L t capture-pane -p -t t; tmux -L t kill-server
+```
+
+## How the code fits together
+
+- **Parser.** Works line by line. `Block open` records which block the previous line belonged
+  to: a paragraph, quote or list item continues only on the next line of the same kind, and a
+  blank line closes it. Source line breaks inside a paragraph stay as `"\n"` in the text,
+  like leaf. Emphasis is flattened: nested `**bold *italic***` becomes plain tokens with
+  `InlineStyle` bits, so every `InlineToken` is one run of text. Table layout, cell wrapping
+  and search depend on that.
+- **Renderer.** Everything prints to `std::cout`. `inlineString()` and `renderRows()` capture
+  it by swapping `std::cout.rdbuf()`, so new output code must go through `std::cout` too.
+- **Widths.** Always measure in terminal columns: `displayWidth()` for plain text,
+  `visibleWidth()` for text containing escapes. Never use `std::string::size()`; Cyrillic,
+  CJK and emoji break it.
+- **Styles after a break.** Styled tokens end with `RESET`. When text is cut into rows,
+  `trackSgr()` carries the active codes over to the next row. Keep that in mind in any new
+  wrapping code.
+- **Pager.** `--watch` on a terminal renders the whole document into screen rows
+  (`renderRows`) and draws a window of them on the alternate screen. `tokenRows` maps
+  tokens to rows for TOC jumps. Leave the terminal in a clean state on every exit path
+  (`leavePager`, also from the signal handlers).
+
+## Conventions
+
+- Keep the style of the surrounding code: 4-space indent, `termstyle::` constants.
+- No new dependencies. POSIX only: Linux, and macOS per the README's brew instructions (only Linux
+  is tested). Windows is not supported.
+- Parser changes come with a check in `tests/parser_test.cpp`.
+- If `--watch` keys change, update `src/utils/cli_info.cpp`.
+
+## Packaging (local)
+
+`pkg/` is ignored through `.git/info/exclude` and holds an Arch `PKGBUILD`. It builds the
+upstream `v1.0.0` tarball with `termmark-tables.patch` applied, which contains every local
+commit since upstream `befa03f` except this file. After committing:
+
+```sh
+git format-patch befa03f..HEAD --stdout -- . ':!AGENTS.md' > pkg/termmark-tables.patch
+cd pkg && sed -i 's/^pkgrel=.*/pkgrel=N/' PKGBUILD && updpkgsums
+```
+
+cmake is not installed on the host, so the package is built in a clean container:
+`archlinux:base-devel` with `pacman -S cmake`, then `makepkg` as a normal user.
-- 
