From eba3d0c20e941db9634ceda953897d1138fd3951 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sfslinux <sfslinux@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:57:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/38] Reflow paragraphs, front matter, code highlighting
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- paragraph, list item and quote lines are joined (CommonMark); two
  trailing spaces still break the line; --no-reflow keeps the source line
  breaks like leaf
- YAML front matter becomes a table filling the width, like leaf: keys as
  header row, or one row per key from 5 keys on; comments skipped, list
  items and "key: >" text joined
- fenced code blocks are highlighted with the highlight module
- a link cut by a row wrap is closed at the row end and reopened on the
  next row
- like leaf: "─" horizontal rule, padded inline code spans (kept whole in
  table cells), underlined "Notes" for footnotes
- cmake builds the C module and runs both tests
