+  standalone C99 module with no TermMark dependencies, meant to be copied into other programs
+  (e.g. l3afpad). Keep it that way: plain C, no C++ and no includes from TermMark. It also
+  compiles as C++. It reports spans per line; the colors live in the renderer
+  (`CodeBlockToken`).
 - **Renderer.** Everything prints to `std::cout`. `inlineString()` and `renderRows()` capture
   it by swapping `std::cout.rdbuf()`, so new output code must go through `std::cout` too.
