Subject: [PATCH 19/38] Colors of leaf's default theme
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

termstyle::theme holds leaf's OceanDark colors (24-bit) and the
base16-ocean.dark syntax colors leaf uses for code; the renderer uses
them everywhere instead of the 16 basic colors:

- text, bold, italic, inline code (orange on dark brown), links
- headings per level, bold (level 6 italic); only levels 1 and 2 are
  underlined, in the dim heading rule color, as in leaf
- quotes, list markers by depth (third level "▸"), ordered and task markers
- tables, horizontal rules, footnote markers and "Notes"
- code blocks: frame, label, gutter, text and syntax colors; true/false/null
  as constants and JSON keys as strings, like base16-ocean
- --watch: search highlights as backgrounds, contents screen with the
  active row background, status bar

Checked against `leaf --inline ansi` escape codes.
