+# Changelog
+
+Changes since the original [TermMark 1.0.0](https://github.com/ishanawal/TermMark/releases/tag/v1.0.0).
+Rendering follows [leaf](https://github.com/RivoLink/leaf) (`leaf --inline`).
+
+## Unreleased
+
+### Added
+
+- Syntax highlighting in code blocks for sh, C/C++, Python, JavaScript/TypeScript, JSON, YAML
+  and INI: keywords, strings, comments, numbers, names (keys, variables, sections) and
+  commands/functions. The highlighter (`include/highlight/highlight.h`,
+  `src/highlight/highlight.c`) is a standalone C99 module that other programs can reuse.
+- `--watch` is a full-screen viewer on a terminal: scrolling, table of contents (`t`), jumps to
+  sections (`1`–`9`), search (`/`, `Ctrl+F`, `n`/`N`), opening the file in an editor
+  (`Ctrl+E`), status bar. Without a terminal it re-renders as before.
+- `--editor CMD` (`-e`): editor for `Ctrl+E`. Default `$VISUAL` or `$EDITOR`, else the first
+  installed of nano, mcedit, vim, vi. Opens at the line on screen; `{$line}` and `{$path}` work
+  as in leaf.
+- `--no-reflow`: keep source line breaks inside paragraphs, like leaf.
+- Markdown: nested lists, task lists, ordered lists starting at any number, setext headings,
+  `***` rules, multi-line quotes, strikethrough, nested emphasis, backslash escapes, code spans
+  with backticks inside, images, autolinks, footnotes, YAML front matter (shown as a table).
+- Tests for the parser and the highlighter (`ctest`).
+- `examples/highlighting.md`, `README.ru.md`, `AGENTS.md`.
+
+### Changed
+
+- Colors of leaf's default theme (24-bit) for text, headings, lists, quotes, tables, code
+  and the viewer.
+- Paragraphs, list items and quotes are word-wrapped to the terminal; their source lines are
+  joined (CommonMark), two trailing spaces keep a line break.
+- Headings: levels 1 and 2 underlined (`═`, `─`) like leaf.
+- Tables: Unicode borders, `╞═╪╡` under the header, lines between rows, column alignment,
+  fitted to the terminal width with word-wrapped cells.
+- Code blocks: closed frame with line numbers, long lines wrapped inside the frame.
+- Inline code is padded, links get a `#` marker, lists use `•`, `◦`, `▸`.
+- Piped output (no terminal) is laid out for 80 columns.
+
+### Fixed
+
+- Tables with alignment colons in the separator row (`|:--|--:|`) were not recognized.
+- Table and code widths were counted in bytes, so Cyrillic, CJK and emoji broke the frames.
+- The last table column was lost when the header had no trailing `|`.
+- Each source line of a paragraph was printed as a separate paragraph.
+- `2 * 3` and `snake_case_names` were turned into italics.
+- Code spans containing backticks, and an unclosed code fence lost their content.
+- The horizontal rule read an uninitialized terminal size when output was piped.
